  "id": "COMPOUND:32820 - PROTEIN:5028",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 14-Hydroxy-9-epi-caryophyllene and COLO-824 through a series of target interactions. The compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including Zanthpodocarpin B and (-)-Clovene, which in turn target COLO-824. Similarly, Prulaurasin, another entity linked to 14-Hydroxy-9-epi-caryophyllene, also targets COLO-824. These findings collectively indicate that 14-Hydroxy-9-epi-caryophyllene may act as a mediator in the signaling pathways leading to COLO-824, possibly through the activation of downstream targets that influence the cell's behavior. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a pathway where 14-Hydroxy-9-epi-caryophyllene may modulate the activity of other compounds, ultimately affecting COLO-824.",
